{"uncertainty": 0.2, "outcome": "rtl_bug", "artifacts": [{"kind": "root_cause_analysis", "title": "Root cause: debounce restarts its stability count only on a rising edge of noisy", "summary": "Traces to [requirement:req-19189b08df]. The design under investigation is [artifact:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.a1]. Its header states the specified behaviour: a change on noisy, in either direction, restarts the count, so a pulse of STABLE edges or fewer, high or low, never reaches clean.\n\nDEFECT: the restart condition is `if (noisy && !prev) cnt <= 0`. That is a rising-edge test only. A falling edge does not reset cnt.\n\nCAUSALITY: suppose noisy has been high long enough that clean=1 and cnt has saturated at STABLE-1=3, and noisy then falls.\n- Edge A (noisy=0, prev=1): the code does not restart the count. cnt is already 3, so it is not incremented and stays 3. clean is not updated because noisy!=prev.\n- Edge B (noisy=0, prev=0): the update condition `noisy==prev && cnt==STABLE-1` is true, so clean<=0 after only 2 low edges.\nThe fault therefore originates at edge A, where the count is not cleared. It becomes visible one edge later as clean falling.\n\nINCORRECTNESS: the specification requires a restart on any change. The correct condition is `noisy != prev`. This fault affects every low-going glitch shorter than STABLE+1 edges that arrives while clean is high. High-going glitches are filtered correctly, which explains why some tests pass.\n\nTRIAGE CONTEXT: VeriTriage gave a low-confidence result and named an RTL bug only as its top hypothesis [evidence:prj-a26914b30e.triage.e1] [run:run-0001]. The triage repro failed 1 of 1 checks and reached $finish [evidence:prj-a26914b30e.triage.e2] [run:run-0002].\n\nHYPOTHESES, RANKED:\n(1) rtl_bug, accepted. It explains the failure from the RTL text alone. It would be refuted if the new repro's glitch check passed on this RTL, or if the restart logic covered falling edges.\n(2) testbench_bug, rejected. I derived the expected value again from the specification clause and did not copy it from RTL output. The new testbench checks only specified behaviour: clean holds through a 2-edge low glitch. It also includes positive checks, a long high and a long low, which this RTL satisfies, so the testbench is not simply failing everything. It would be refuted if this testbench failed on clean RTL as well; that is the scorer's clean-input run, which I have not seen.\n(3) infrastructure, rejected but not fully excluded. The triage run built, reached $finish and reported a check failure, not a tool error [run:run-0002]. The mechanism is deterministic and visible in the source. A clean rebuild was not performed by me. It would be refuted by a nondeterministic or build-dependent result.\n(4) spec_ambiguity, rejected. The clause explicitly says 'in either direction' and 'high or low', so it fixes the behaviour. A residual risk is that the only specification available is the file's own header comment. It would be refuted by a separate specification permitting rise-only restart.\n\nREPRO: the companion testbench tb/debounce_rca_repro_tb.v is expected to fail its glitch check on this RTL and pass on a both-edge-restart RTL. That expectation is to be confirmed by the platform's simulator.run gate."}], "files": [{"path": "tb/debounce_rca_repro_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Self-checking repro: a short low glitch must not reach clean", "summary": "Minimal self-checking repro for [artifact:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.a1], serving [requirement:req-19189b08df]. It has 4 checks, all taken from the specification clause in the RTL header.\n1. clean is low after reset.\n2. A long high on noisy reaches clean.\n3. A 2-edge low glitch never drops clean. This check is expected to fail on the rise-only-restart RTL.\n4. A long low on noisy reaches clean.\nIt reads nirmaan_nonce and prints exactly one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict just before $finish. It uses only the debounce port interface, with no internal names.", "entry": "debounce_rca_repro_tb"}], "tool_runs": ["run-0001", "run-0002"], "claims": ["The new testbench is expected to report 3 passed, 1 failed on debounce_rise_only_restart.v and 4 passed, 0 failed on an RTL that restarts the count on any change of noisy; neither run has been performed by me.", "The fix is expected to be replacing `noisy && !prev` with `noisy != prev` in the restart condition; this fix has not been simulated.", "Independent review of this root-cause analysis has not yet been recorded; the existing review_record covers the RTL fixture, not this analysis."], "escalation": null, "notes": "I could not see the triage testbench's content or the regression log, so this diagnosis rests on the RTL text and its header specification. Uncertainty is 0.2 for three reasons: the specification is only the header comment, I have not seen the clean reference RTL, and no clean-rebuild experiment was available to me. Review is still required before approval, per P6."}

=== FILE: tb/debounce_rca_repro_tb.v ===
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
// Repro for the debounce regression failure.
// Specified behaviour (debounce header): a change on `noisy`, in either
// direction, restarts the stability count, so a pulse of STABLE edges or
// fewer, high or low, never reaches `clean`.
// This bench drives a 2-edge LOW glitch while `clean` is high; `clean` must
// stay high. Expected values come from the specification, not from RTL output.
module debounce_rca_repro_tb;
    reg clk   = 1'b0;
    reg rst   = 1'b1;
    reg noisy = 1'b0;
    wire clean;

    integer passed = 0;
    integer failed = 0;
    integer i;
    reg dropped;
    reg [8*64-1:0] nonce;

    debounce #(.STABLE(4)) dut (
        .clk  (clk),
        .rst  (rst),
        .noisy(noisy),
        .clean(clean)
    );

    always #5 clk = ~clk;

    initial begin
        if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce))
            nonce = "none";

        // Reset; inputs change and are sampled on negedge.
        rst   = 1'b1;
        noisy = 1'b0;
        repeat (3) @(posedge clk);
        @(negedge clk) rst = 1'b0;

        // Check 1: clean is low after reset.
        @(negedge clk);
        if (clean === 1'b0) passed = passed + 1;
        else begin failed = failed + 1; $display("CHECK 1 FAIL: clean=%b after reset, expected 0", clean); end

        // Check 2: a long stable high reaches clean.
        noisy = 1'b1;
        repeat (10) @(negedge clk);
        if (clean === 1'b1) passed = passed + 1;
        else begin failed = failed + 1; $display("CHECK 2 FAIL: clean=%b after long high, expected 1", clean); end

        // Check 3: a 2-edge low glitch (well under STABLE=4) never reaches clean.
        dropped = 1'b0;
        noisy = 1'b0;
        for (i = 0; i < 2; i = i + 1) begin
            @(negedge clk);
            if (clean !== 1'b1) dropped = 1'b1;
        end
        noisy = 1'b1;
        for (i = 0; i < 10; i = i + 1) begin
            @(negedge clk);
            if (clean !== 1'b1) dropped = 1'b1;
        end
        if (!dropped) passed = passed + 1;
        else begin failed = failed + 1; $display("CHECK 3 FAIL: 2-edge low glitch reached clean, expected clean to stay 1"); end

        // Check 4: a long stable low reaches clean.
        noisy = 1'b0;
        repeat (10) @(negedge clk);
        if (clean === 1'b0) passed = passed + 1;
        else begin failed = failed + 1; $display("CHECK 4 FAIL: clean=%b after long low, expected 0", clean); end

        $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed);
        $finish;
    end
endmodule
=== END FILE ===
